Central system-library download hook (prototype for an upstream proposal).

Wraps the body of ly_download_associated_package() -- the single choke
point every bundled-3rdParty download funnels through (the generic
3rdParty dependency loop, the BuiltInPackages ZLIB bootstrap, and both
LYWrappers branches all call it, then call
find_package(<name> REQUIRED MODULE)) -- in a per-package opt-out:
when -DLY_USE_SYSTEM_<NAME>=ON is passed, the bundled download is
skipped and the trailing find_package resolves a system Find module
from CMAKE_MODULE_PATH (our Find<X>.cmake shims) instead.

This replaces Patch0006's per-line gating of every ly_associate_package
entry in BuiltInPackages_linux_x86_64.cmake with one ~10-line change to
core machinery that rarely churns. Behavior is byte-identical for any
package whose flag is not set (Python, Qt, AWSNativeSDK, ... keep
downloading exactly as before).

Two notes:
- find_library_name is uppercased before the flag check so the existing
  uppercase flag spellings (LY_USE_SYSTEM_LUA, ...) match mixed-case
  target names (Lua, RapidJSON, ZLIB, ...).
- The hook keys per TARGET while the per-line gate keyed per PACKAGE.
  The one multi-target association (OpenEXR-3.1.3 declares TARGETS
  OpenEXR Imath) therefore needs LY_USE_SYSTEM_IMATH passed alongside
  LY_USE_SYSTEM_OPENEXR, which the spec now does.

Gated behind the swap_hook bcond; exercised on the o3de-experimental
channel as the validation for the upstream "add a hook / standardize it"
conversation with nick-l-o3de (2026-06-03). If upstream adopts this (or
the explicit per-line alternative), Patch0006 retires entirely.

--- a/cmake/3rdPartyPackages.cmake
+++ b/cmake/3rdPartyPackages.cmake
@@ -710,10 +710,20 @@
 # is brought into scope (and if necessary, downloaded.)
 macro(ly_download_associated_package find_library_name)
     unset(package_name)
-    ly_get_package_association(${find_library_name} package_name)
-    if (package_name)
-        # it is an associated package.
-        ly_enable_package(${package_name})
+    # System-library override: when LY_USE_SYSTEM_<NAME> is ON (NAME being the
+    # uppercased find_library_name), skip the bundled-package download entirely
+    # and let the caller's find_package(<find_library_name> REQUIRED MODULE)
+    # resolve a system Find module from CMAKE_MODULE_PATH instead. Opt-in per
+    # package: anything without a flag set (e.g. Python) downloads exactly as
+    # before. Uppercasing keeps one flag spelling (LY_USE_SYSTEM_LUA) working
+    # for mixed-case target names (Lua, RapidJSON, ZLIB, ...).
+    string(TOUPPER "${find_library_name}" ly_download_associated_package_name_upper)
+    if (NOT LY_USE_SYSTEM_${ly_download_associated_package_name_upper})
+        ly_get_package_association(${find_library_name} package_name)
+        if (package_name)
+            # it is an associated package.
+            ly_enable_package(${package_name})
+        endif()
     endif()
 endmacro()
 
